WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:06.552
Hi! Today you learn the imperative.

2
00:00:06.952 --> 00:00:09.912
With du, ihr and Sie.

3
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:17.920
Three forms, one verb. With du: no du and no st:

4
00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:20.392
Come!

5
00:00:20.792 --> 00:00:25.144
With ihr: like ihr kommt, but without ihr:

6
00:00:25.544 --> 00:00:30.064
Come! And with Sie: Kommen Sie!

7
00:00:31.767 --> 00:00:34.799
With e to i, the i stays:

8
00:00:35.199 --> 00:00:38.735
You take. Take!

9
00:00:39.135 --> 00:00:42.911
But with a to ä, the umlaut goes:

10
00:00:43.311 --> 00:00:46.871
You drive. Drive!

11
00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:54.431
The imperative is direct. With bitte it's friendly:

12
00:00:54.831 --> 00:00:57.623
Please turn on the light!

13
00:00:58.023 --> 00:01:01.463
And with doch or mal it sounds nicer:

14
00:01:01.863 --> 00:01:04.007
Why don't you come along!

15
00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:10.508
Listen: Lena and Mateo make pancakes.

16
00:01:10.908 --> 00:01:13.604
Please pass me the eggs!

17
00:01:14.004 --> 00:01:16.484
Here you are.

18
00:01:16.884 --> 00:01:20.396
Take the milk and stir!

19
00:01:20.796 --> 00:01:22.868
Like this?

20
00:01:23.268 --> 00:01:29.276
Yes! Be careful!

21
00:01:29.676 --> 00:01:32.900
Mmm, that smells good!

22
00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:43.464
Now you! Give a friend three tips for learning German. Use the imperative!

23
00:01:55.167 --> 00:01:59.303
Great! Now you can:

24
00:01:59.703 --> 00:02:06.767
You make requests and give tips – with du, ihr and Sie. And always with bitte!

25
00:02:07.167 --> 00:02:09.287
See you soon!
